Z||000000||flexableface||05-17-2000||11:51 AM||||hello i was think about put a shift kit in my trans. It is a automaitic. I was wondering if anyone has put a shift kit in there trans and how did you like it. i was thinking about ordering from the fiero. Should i order it there or is there a better place. <BR>              thanks luke||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-17-2000||12:00 PM||||My car has the "trans-go" Shift kit in it. It was in the car when I bought it (the paperwork for the kit and the receipt from the shop that installed it was in the car when I bought it). It works very well. The shifts are very positive and I haven't had any problems with it. (had car for 5 years) I think the kit was originally from IRM and cost $40.00 but I don't know if it is still available from them. Just E-mail them at: IRMFIERO@aol.com  or call them at 1-800-367-8423.||||reg||1
Z||000002||flexableface||05-17-2000||12:13 PM||||i was also wondering if put ford trans fluid in would get more postive shifts because the ford fluid is a difference velocity??||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||05-17-2000||11:24 PM||||good way to really screw up a tranny is put the wrong fluid in. Even Ford no longer uses Type-F, also called Mercon, fluid. (I forget what year Ford changed to Dexron. Sometime in the 80's.)<P>pump down the tranny and put DexronIII and a new filter in. That alone will change shifting. You may have to adjust the TV cable a wee bit if you got any where near 6+ quarts of new fluid in. DexronIII is compatible with all GM trannys since 1940 something but it is a tad diferant viscosity.<P>Trans-Go kits and all other TH125c parts are available from the Transmission Exchange Co. Look them up with HotBot. I think a complete rebuild kit was less than $100. The shift kit was around $20 last time I called, maybe less. I doubt anyone can beat their prices if they can even get the parts.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-17-2000).]||||reg||1
